From: Prabhsimran Singh <prabhsimrans@nvidia.com>
Subject: ggml: DFLASH_CONV op for the DFlash2 drafter's dynamic grouped convolution

The DFlash2 drafter mixes each token with the k - 1 tokens before it inside its block of drafted positions, with
per-token coefficients predicted by the drafter: y[h, t] = sum_j (coef[h / group, j, t] + base[h, j]) * x[h, t - j].
Built from generic ops this is k shifted views, broadcast adds and multiplies per layer; ggml_dflash_conv does it in
one op. The CUDA kernel runs one thread per (channel, token) with the taps unrolled for k <= 4; coef and base take any
strides, so the drafter's projections feed it without copies. There is no CPU path (the drafter runs on CUDA only).

Upstream: candidate for upstream's DFlash2 drafter, which builds this from generic ops (needs a CPU implementation and
test-backend-ops cases).

